{"parentUuid":"f1d5a382-6379-40c4-8582-ce962b6b4621","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0b81aa46-3ac1-41a7-bee9-ff3aba05ec92","agentId":"ac44742970c7341bd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0181cMVDMDDPPQqLmAHt64w6","type":"tool_result","content":"746-the body. Deliberate deviation from the classical PNF patterns is also encouraged in applying non-impact \n747:plyometrics, since this develops a wider range of more demanding functional motor abilities that typify sport.\n748-Thus, from the realm of martial arts alone, one may borrow thrust punches, rising blocks, downward blocks, \n749-knife-hand thrusts, palm-heel strikes, front kicks, side snap kicks, side thrust kicks, front kicks and many other \n18:The same idea appears earlier for speed-strength: \"good results are achieved by making the special exercise more demanding\", e.g. \"water resistance in rowing or very small loads on the limbs of track-and-field athletes and gymnasts\" (PDF pp. 277-278 / printed pp. 266-267; that passage belongs to 5.2.3).\n28:**Related** — [[framework--five-criteria-of-dynamic-correspondence]]; [[claim--parachute-resistance-tradeoffs-for-dynamic-correspondence]]; [[heuristic--parachute-resistance-sizing-progression-and-contrast-release]]; [[framework--strength-endurance-taxonomy-and-absolute-vs-partial]] (Ch3.2.2, \"execute the competition exercises themselves under demanding conditions\"); [[case-study--soviet-sport-specific-strength-endurance-prescriptions]]","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"51bb0d86-7f59-47c2-97f6-8c1efb8730af","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:27:49.439Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"746-the body. Deliberate deviation from the classical PNF patterns is also encouraged in applying non-impact \n747:plyometrics, since this develops a wider range of more demanding functional motor abilities that typify sport.\n748-Thus, from the realm of martial arts alone, one may borrow thrust punches, rising blocks, downward blocks, \n749-knife-hand thrusts, palm-heel strikes, front kicks, side snap kicks, side thrust kicks, front kicks and many other \n18:The same idea appears earlier for speed-strength: \"good results are achieved by making the special exercise more demanding\", e.g. \"water resistance in rowing or very small loads on the limbs of track-and-field athletes and gymnasts\" (PDF pp. 277-278 / printed pp. 266-267; that passage belongs to 5.2.3).\n28:**Related** — [[framework--five-criteria-of-dynamic-correspondence]]; [[claim--parachute-resistance-tradeoffs-for-dynamic-correspondence]]; [[heuristic--parachute-resistance-sizing-progression-and-contrast-release]]; [[framework--strength-endurance-taxonomy-and-absolute-vs-partial]] (Ch3.2.2, \"execute the competition exercises themselves under demanding conditions\"); [[case-study--soviet-sport-specific-strength-endurance-prescriptions]]","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f1d5a382-6379-40c4-8582-ce962b6b4621","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
