{"parentUuid":"fe41ac4f-dd69-440c-b547-e14bb7979c41","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ac44742970c7341bd","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cffd2pi98XXBsDf6aQLT9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Writing the report."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":421,"cache_read_input_tokens":199626,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":421,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":4,"requestId":"req_011Cffd2fLKzU2RrcpxSEqap","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"c1441591-81aa-4dbc-85a8-f8cd192d4ccc","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:32:28.858Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
{"parentUuid":"c1441591-81aa-4dbc-85a8-f8cd192d4ccc","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ac44742970c7341bd","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cffd2pi98XXBsDf6aQLT9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YVxukNj4oFTT7g6eQ3DJpr","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch5b_opus_round2.md","content":"# Review round 2: Supertraining Ch 5 batch 5b (5.2.4-5.2.5), Opus independent reviewer\n\nScope: the 30 files in `staging/_scope_supertraining_ch5b.txt`. Inputs: round-1 review `staging/review_supertraining_ch5b_opus.md` and fix log `staging/fixes_supertraining_ch5b_applied.md`. My job was to falsify: check that each round-1 fix landed and is correct, and that no fix added a new error.\n\nSource: `staging/books/supertraining-6th-expanded.pdf`, PDF idx = printed + 11. I extracted the text layer of PDF 233 and 278-299 (`staging/_tmp/r2_5b_text.txt`) and rendered the same pages to `staging/_renders/r2_5b_p<N>.png`, plus page-break crops `r2_5b_p292_crop.png` and `r2_5b_p293_crop.png`. **Opened as images:** PDF 281, 282, 284, 285, 286, 287, 288, 289, 292 (crop), 293 (crop), 296, 297, 299. **Text layer only:** PDF 233, 277-278 (5.2.3 link), 280, 283, 293-294 (squat rule). I also checked every quoted string in the 30 files against the text layer by script, with fuzzy matching for OCR noise. Every miss was OCR noise, a figure label (checked on the image) or a non-source quote (baseline, Inference).\n\nSummary: **28 GO, 2 FIX, 0 NO-GO.** All 13 round-1 FIX items and the Wilson note landed and are correct against the pages. One fix added a new wording error (475-jumps, \"untested\"). One round-1 GO entry (weekly frequency) cites baseline line 105 as Eric's \"stated rule\" without the tag that the fixer added to the same line elsewhere.\n\n## Entry table\n\n| File | Verdict | Problem / what I checked | Exact correction |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| claim--high-volume-plyometrics-do-not-build-rebound-fatigue-resistance | GO | Fix 1 landed: `confidence: supported`; the conflict block is now one sentence pointing to brief-max. Both Nicol quotes checked on the images of PDF 280 and PDF 288-289. Line 122 quote is exact and tagged Explicit. Nothing new is wrong. | None. |\n| heuristic--plyometric-surface-footwear-and-simple-apparatus | GO | Fix 2 landed: `supported`, and the different-aims Inference is labelled. On the PDF 289 image the \"as alluded to earlier ... soft-soled shoes and very resilient jumping surfaces\" sentence sits right before the sand finding (Montagni & Cardinale, 1996, 5 days). Swing (rope length sets oscillation time) and Pogo-Stick (\"height of rebound\") match PDF 289. Footwear sentence matches the PDF 284 image. \"suitably firm shock-absorbing surfaces\" matches the PDF 288 image. | None. |\n| heuristic--strength-endurance-load-tempo-and-the-75-80-percent-ceiling | GO | Fix 3 landed. On the PDF 297 image: skaters \"80-85% of 1RM\", 4-12 reps to complete fatigue, 2-4 min (Mikhailov & Panov, 1975); rowers \"50-80%\" (Ulrich et al, 1966). The new specificity quote matches the PDF 296 image (\"carry-over\" is hyphenated across a line break). The 8 determinants, 25-50%, 60-120/min, 60% and the 75-80% ceiling (Zatsiorsky, 1966) are on PDF 296. Baseline quotes: line 116 \"worst case scenario\" (Explicit) and line 117 \"staff do program it in the off-season\" (Explicit, Q19) are exact. | None. |\n| heuristic--brief-maximal-tension-vs-plyometrics-by-resistance-size | GO | Fix 4 landed. (1) The line 76 tag is verbatim: \"[contested; the ratio tracks IMTP strength; one controlled trial (Pleša 2024, basketball, split at 0.90) supported only the strength arm; no football data]\". The Q21 quote is exact. The \"Tension 17 ... (line 261)\" pointer is correct; line 261 is Tension 17. (2) The Example now quotes PDF 289 and no longer says \"jumping from depth\". (3) The novice caveat matches the PDF 299 image: within-workout experiment, \"pauses ... increased slightly\", \"There was no statistically significant difference\", largest increase \"in the third group\" (depth jumps). The across-stage experiment (\"the first variant was more effective\") and \"the validity of this hypothesis can be established conclusively only by careful experimentation\" are also there. The 40% / 30% / 80% figures and both contested sentences check on the PDF 288-289 images. | None. |\n| claim--depth-jump-training-beat-higher-volume-traditional-training-in-jumpers | **FIX** | Fix 5 landed: the title says \"93 Tons\" and the 5c link is added. The numbers check on the PDF 288 image (475 jumps, 12 weeks, 1472 push-offs, 90-95% / 70-80% / 30-40%, 93 tons). **New error added by the fix:** When NOT says \"The resistance-first rule is untested for novices:\", then cites the PDF 299 experiment, which tested it on novices and found \"no statistically significant difference\". The sentence contradicts itself, and the brief-max entry, fixed in the same round, correctly says \"not supported for novices\". (Round 1 suggested \"untested\"; the fixer followed it.) | Replace \"The resistance-first rule is untested for novices:\" with \"The resistance-first rule is not supported for novices:\". |\n| heuristic--depth-jump-height-set-by-transition-speed-and-heel-contact | GO | Fix 6 landed. The line 74 quote \"was deliberately chosen as the daily athlete-readiness marker\" is exact and tagged Explicit; the drop-jump RSI idea is labelled Inference. \"using considerably lower jump heights with anyone who is unused to this type of training\" is on PDF 233 (text layer; 233 - 11 = printed 222, locator correct). Items 1, 5 and 8 and the \"strength fitness\" sentence check on the images of PDF 285-287. The Fig 5.10 description matches the PDF 286 image (\"Horizontal Projection\" over two variants, \"Vertical Projection\" with a hanging marker). | None. |\n| heuristic--maximal-plyometric-and-depth-jump-volume-and-rest | GO | Fix 7 landed. Item 1 is out of Model 2 and labelled Inference. The PDF 286 image prints \"1-15 minutes\". The PDF 287 image shows Fig 5.11 with no box: vertical, tuck, split and reach-to-marker jumps. Voices are labelled per item, which the page supports. Item 2 (4×10, 2-3×5-8, 10-15 min easy running), item 3 (3×/week, 2×10), item 4 (5-8 reps) and item 6 (~10 min) check on the PDF 285-286 images. Model 1 (2-4 min, 10-12 min) checks on PDF 283 (text layer). \"over 100\" checks on PDF 293. Baseline: the line 105 quote is exact, with tag \"Inferred (transcript + shared slides)\" and \"Not claimed in the interview\"; the line 186 quote is exact with tag Explicit (Q15). | Optional: after the 72-hour Inference, add \"the book's own in-season limit is stricter: no depth jumps within 10 days of competition (item 5, PDF 286; see [[heuristic--depth-jump-weekly-frequency-and-seasonal-placement]])\". The Inference is labelled and true, but a reader could take 72 h as the operative rule. |\n| framework--five-phases-of-a-plyometric-action | GO | Fix 8 landed: \"The caption words the EM delay differently\", then both quotes, then \"Inference: both describe the electrical-to-mechanical interval\"; \"does not reconcile\" is gone. Caption and item 2 match the PDF 281 image. The Fig 5.5 description (boxes, EM delay, eccentric and concentric bars, \"Explosive Isometrics / Coupling Time\") matches. | None. |\n| framework--plyometric-training-classification-impact-intensity-and-function | GO | Fix 9 landed: no \"the authors\" left; voice is Siff, using \"powermetrics\". The Fig 5.8 description matches the PDF 284 image box for box, including \"Preparatory/Supplementary Activities\" over \"Weight Training\" and \"Jumps Throws Etc\". The new F = ma paragraph is verbatim on the PDF 284 image. The note that no study is given is correct. The [[principle--equal-force-different-loading-methods]] link resolves. | None. |\n| heuristic--rate-plyometric-intensity-by-contact-momentum-from-drop-height | GO | Fix 9 landed: Siff voice for the PDF 283 scale, \"the authors'\" for items 1 and 4. Items 1 and 4 match the PDF 285 image. The new Fig 5.9 paragraph matches the PDF 285 image: caption exact; drop push-ups between blocks; pulley and weight-stack pushes, pulls, squat pull, kicks, overhead pull, seated row; incline-board work; seated kick at a suspended object beside a wall pad. It is marked approximate. The weight-stack free-fall reading is labelled Inference. Physics re-checked: m√(2gh) at 100 kg is 313 and 443 kg·m/s, ratio √2. | None. |\n| claim--lewis-formula-estimates-jump-power-from-bodymass-and-height | GO | Fix 10 landed: the Inference in the title is labelled; line 77 carries its verbatim tag \"Inferred (protocol; author uncertain)\" (disagreement 5 justified). Formula \"(21.693) B√H\" matches the PDF 288 image. 21.693 = 9.8 × √4.9 re-checked. | None. |\n| claim--plyometric-injury-risk-comes-from-prescription-not-the-method | GO | Fix 11 landed. The PDF 281 image shows the right-margin cut: \"adequ\", \"running a\", \"te\", \"wi\". The bracketed restorations are marked. The new \"drills ... militarism\" bullet matches the image and is labelled Siff. On PDF 280 (text layer): \"Siff's former colleague, Dr Mark Swanepoel, at the University of the Witwatersrand\", the five cartilage cites and Swanepoel 1998. | None. |\n| heuristic--resisted-and-water-plyometrics | GO | Fix 12 landed. The crops show \"No resistance\" at the foot of PDF 292 and \"methods should not use heavy weights or stiff elastic cords during depth jumps\" at the head of PDF 293. The (sic) note and the Inference label are correct. The aqua sentences match the PDF 293 image. | None. |\n| claim--prestretch-benefit-decay-time-differs-by-task | GO | The Wilson source note is correct (see the Wilson section below). On the PDF 281 image the text gives \"Wilson et al (1990) ... 4 seconds\". PDF 282 gives Chapman & Caldwell 0.25 s, \"Wilson et al (1991) ... 0.37 second\" and the Fig 5.6 caption \"based on the data of Wilson et al, 1991\". Fig 5.6 readings agree with the image: about 50% near 0.8-1 s, about 80% at 2 s, near 100% at about 4 s. Fig 5.7 is near-linear over 0.1-0.25 s. `contested` is kept and is justified (\"apparent contradiction\", PDF 282). | None. |\n| heuristic--depth-jump-weekly-frequency-and-seasonal-placement | **FIX** | Spot check: items 3, 4 and 5 match the PDF 286 image (once or twice a week; 3×/week, 2×10; 3-4 days; 10-14 days; 10 days). Item 15 (5-6 days) matches the PDF 287 image. **Problem:** \"Eric's baseline: 'In-season, the stated rule is \"maintain intensity, reduce volume\"' (`docs/method-baseline.md` line 105)\" has no tag. Line 105 is **Inferred (transcript + shared slides)**, and the baseline adds \"Not claimed in the interview\". With no tag, an inferred, unclaimed line reads as Eric's stated rule, which is the attribution failure this gate exists to catch. The fixer tagged the same quote in the volume-and-rest entry. | After \"(`docs/method-baseline.md` line 105\" insert \", Inferred (transcript + shared slides); the baseline adds \\\"Not claimed in the interview\\\"\". Optional, from round 1: also cite line 186 (Explicit, Q15: \"lifting and hard practice end 72 hours before a Saturday game\"). |\n| case-study--soviet-sport-specific-strength-endurance-prescriptions | GO | Spot check on the PDF 297 image: Chistyakov 65%; Likachyevskaya & Kovalchuk 55-60% bodymass, 8-10 times, 60-85%, one-third bodymass for 18-20 reps, squats 55-60% to fatigue; Popov 60-80%; skaters 80-85%, 4-12 reps, 2-4 min, 15-25 reps, 3-5 sets, 5-8 min; rowers 50-80% and 30-40%; Chumakova 18-20 kg, 40%, 35-50 kg, 2-3 reps, 28%; squats +20-30 a week, from 50 to 200-300 reps over 2-3 months. All match. | None. |\n| claim--zatsiorsky-and-hansen-show-strength-endurance-training-specificity | GO | Spot check on the PDF 296 image: 84%, 10 times a day, 5 weeks, 60%, 93%, \"28 repetitions per minute\" (faint first digit, reads 28), 5 s tension and 2 s rest, 219%. The Hansen 1963 sentence runs onto PDF 297 (image). All match. | None. |\n| claim--depth-landings-from-2-to-3-2-m-produce-forces-over-20-times-bodyweight | GO | Spot check on the PDF 288 image: Dursenev and Raevsky (1978), \"2m or more\", \"soft gymnastic mats\", 0.028-0.061 secs, 1500-3500 kgf, \"over 20 times bodyweight\", \"up to 3.2 metres\", the inadvisable-3.2 m caveat, \"limit the number of drops per session\", \"suitably firm shock-absorbing surfaces\". All match. | Optional, from round 1, still open: \"holds for a 75 kg subject\" would read better as \"needs a bodymass under 75 kg at 1500 kgf\". |\n| heuristic--preparatory-progression-before-depth-jumps | GO | Spot check on the PDF 286-288 images: item 1 \"several months\" and the contra-indications; item 6 \"about 25 repetitions\" then \"about 20\"; item 7 skipping; items 13-14; the eccentric and explosive-isometric bullet; front and back squats; static start; upper-body transfer on PDF 288. Line 101 quotes (\"each level a required foundation for the next\", \"compass\") are exact. | None. Optional consistency: add the line 101 tag \"Explicit (interview 2026-09-28, Q1)\". |\n| claim--squat-1-5-to-2-bodymass-rule-applies-to-maximal-depth-jumps-only | GO | Spot check on the PDF 293 text layer: \"squat 1.5-2 times bodymass\", \"rightly criticize\", \"can easily exceed 6 times bodyweight\", \"never intended to apply religiously to submaximal plyometrics\". All match. | None. |\n| heuristic--depth-jump-execution-cues-landing-gaze-breath | GO | Partial spot check on the images of PDF 284-287: landing \"slightly flexed ... balls of the feet\", item 2 posture, item 3 warm-up, item 9 gaze, item 10 \"falling in a relaxed state\", item 12 breath held, and \"Forced exhalation\" on PDF 284. All match. | None. |\n| claim--heavy-squats-and-light-fast-lifts-miss-the-eccentric-concentric-switch | GO | Round-1 GO stands. Not re-checked against page images in round 2. Its quotes match the text layer (OCR-level), and the line 104 quote is exact. | Optional consistency: add the line 104 tag \"Inferred (transcript + slides)\". |\n| claim--popular-plyometric-drills-work-through-other-mechanisms | GO | Round-1 GO stands. The PDF 293 part was checked on the crop image (Chu 1992; Radcliffe & Farantinos 1985; medicine-ball sentence). Quotes match the text layer. | Optional, from round 1: \"p. 294 from the text layer\" to \"verified\" (round 1 opened it). |\n| claim--strength-endurance-hypertrophy-and-cyclic-endurance | GO | Round-1 GO stands. Maisuradze 25%, Maison & Broeker, McMorris & Elkins, R = 0.77 (Zhalei 1964) seen on the PDF 297 image. The Ch4 quote is outside the extracted range and was not re-checked. | None. |\n| claim--plyometric-skill-is-cognitive-and-state-dependent | GO | Round-1 GO stands. Quotes match the PDF 294-295 text layer (OCR-level). Not re-checked against page images in round 2. | None. |\n| framework--non-impact-plyometrics-ericson-and-martial-arts | GO | Round-1 GO stands. The 1994 NSCA sentence and the martial-arts list were seen on the PDF 292 crop. Quotes match the text layer. | None. |\n| framework--shock-methods-to-break-training-stagnation | GO | Round-1 GO stands. The 8 methods and the caution sentence were seen on the PDF 296 image. | None. |\n| heuristic--plyometric-training-coupling-under-0-15-s-feedforward-and-force-time-pattern | GO | Round-1 GO stands. Quotes match the text layer. The line 96 quote is exact. | Optional consistency: add the line 96 tag \"Inferred (transcript)\". |\n| heuristic--match-plyometric-drills-to-limb-symmetry-and-rotational-dominance | GO | Round-1 GO stands. The asymmetric-plyometrics opening was seen on the PDF 289 image. Quotes match the text layer. | None. |\n| heuristic--strength-endurance-under-demanding-sport-like-conditions | GO | Round-1 GO stands. Popov 1966, Zhilei 1964, Chuprun 1966, 57.1%, 27.8% and 9.1% were seen on the PDF 297 image. The 5.2.3 quote (\"good results are achieved by making the special exercise more demanding\", \"water resistance in rowing ...\") was checked on the PDF 277-278 text layer. | None. |\n\n## Wilson source note (prestretch entry)\n\n- **The reference exists.** PubMed PMID 2020276: Wilson GJ, Elliott BC, Wood GA. \"The effect on performance of imposing a delay during a stretch-shorten cycle movement.\" *Med Sci Sports Exerc*. 1991 Mar;23(3):364-70. I pulled it through NCBI E-utilities, not the fixer's route.\n- **The entry claims no more than the abstract supports.** The abstract gives twelve experienced male weight lifters, bench press at 95% of maximum, pause periods imposed between the downward and upward phases, and decay \"accurately described ... by a negative exponential equation with a half-life of 0.85 s.\" It gives no 4 s figure and no 0.37 s figure. The entry says each of these.\n- **The Fig 5.6 match is labelled.** \"Inference: the 0.85 s half-life matches the Fig 5.6 curve ... probably the bench-press study ... would make the caption's 1991 right and the text's '1990' wrong.\" On the image the curve crosses 50% at roughly 0.8-1 s, so the Inference holds. One more check: an exponential with a 0.85 s half-life is about 96% decayed at 4 s, which fits the near-100% at about 4 s in the figure.\n- **Nothing is overstated.** The note says the 0.37 s Wilson (1991) result was not checked, and it leaves `contested` in place on the book's own \"apparent contradiction\".\n\n## Confidence changes\n\n| Entry | Change | Justified by the page? |\n|---|---|---|\n| high-volume-plyometrics | contested to supported | Yes. The Nicol (1997) claim is stated the same way twice (PDF 280; PDF 288). The \"futile ... predominantly\" vs \"main method\" clash (PDF 289) is about explosive strength, not fatigue resistance, and is kept in brief-max. One undescribed citation fits `supported`. |\n| surface-footwear | contested to supported | Yes. On PDF 289 the sand finding opens with \"as alluded to earlier ... soft-soled shoes and very resilient jumping surfaces\", so the author places the two side by side on purpose. The mats belong to a no-rebound landing study (PDF 288). No other library source is cited against it. |\n| 75-80% ceiling | conflict narrowed to skaters | Yes. On PDF 297 the skaters' 80-85% is above the ceiling, and the rowers' 50-80% reaches only its edge. `contested` stays on the skater conflict alone, which is real. |\n\n## Fixer disagreements\n\n1. **Upper-body transfer is already captured.** Justified. `heuristic--preparatory-progression-before-depth-jumps.md` line 23 holds the PDF 288 medicine-ball, press-up and bench-press sentence.\n2. **The novice caveat is scoped to the within-workout experiment.** Justified. PDF 299 has three findings: order \"has no real significance for novices\" across the preparatory period; the across-stage weights-then-depth-jumps variant \"was more effective\"; and the within-workout test found \"no statistically significant difference\". The fixer's wording is more accurate than round 1's. The one slip is the leftover word \"untested\" in the 475 entry (FIX above).\n3. **Item 1 is read as ground jumps by Inference, not fact.** Justified. \"Each exercise\" can grammatically take in the depth jumps, and Fig 5.11 shows no box.\n4. **Voice is labelled per item, not per model.** Justified. Items 4 and 6 sit in the PDF 285 prescription list. The PDF 286 list says \"Prolific experience\" and carries no citation; only its figures are credited to Verkhoshansky (1977).\n5. **The full line 77 tag is used.** Justified; it is verbatim.\n6. **Tags were added to every baseline citation in the edited files.** Every tag checked against method-baseline.md: 74 Explicit, 76 Explicit (Q21) plus its bracket tag, 77 Inferred (protocol; author uncertain), 105 Inferred (transcript + shared slides), 116 Explicit, 117 Explicit (Q19), 122 Explicit, 186 Explicit (Q15). All exact. The fixer did not extend this to the unedited files, which is why the weekly-frequency row is FIX.\n7. **Round-1 optional items for GO files were not applied.** Acceptable under the flagged-files-only rule. The line 105 tag in weekly frequency was more than cosmetic, so it is raised to FIX here.\n\n## Mechanical checks (all 30 files)\n\n- Wikilinks: 160 checked, all resolve in the staging library or the vault. None is wrapped across lines.\n- Section headers: all 30 files have each of the six headers exactly once, in the `**X** —` form.\n- Em dashes outside headers: 0. Titles: 0.\n- Review-history wording: 0. A keyword scan flagged 5 lines; all are ordinary prose (\"fixed function\", \"a corrected value\", \"not fixed by drop height\").\n- CR line endings: 0.\n\n## For the coordinator (outside scope, not a verdict item)\n\n- `case-study--novice-strength-and-speed-strength-sequencing-experiments.md` (5c) already links back to the 475-jumps entry. It does not link to `heuristic--brief-maximal-tension-vs-plyometrics-by-resistance-size`, which now cites it. Add that reciprocal link.\n\n## Overall verdict\n\n**GO AFTER FIXES.** Two one-line fixes:\n1. `claim--depth-jump-training-beat-higher-volume-traditional-training-in-jumpers.md`: change \"untested for novices\" to \"not supported for novices\".\n2. `heuristic--depth-jump-weekly-frequency-and-seasonal-placement.md`: tag the line 105 citation \"Inferred (transcript + shared slides); the baseline adds \\\"Not claimed in the interview\\\"\".\n\nAfter those two, the batch is ready to promote. Neither needs another full review round; a grep confirming both strings is enough.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1723,"cache_read_input_tokens":399673,"output_tokens":9108,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":357},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":421},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":111,"cache_read_input_tokens":199626,"cache_creation_input_tokens":421,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":421,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"},{"input_tokens":201987,"output_tokens":7938,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"advisor_message","model":"claude-fable-5-1"},{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8997,"cache_read_input_tokens":200047,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1302,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1302,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01YVxukNj4oFTT7g6eQ3DJpr":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch5b_opus_round2.md","content":"# Review round 2: Supertraining Ch 5 batch 5b (5.2.4-5.2.5), Opus independent reviewer\n\nScope: the 30 files in `staging/_scope_supertraining_ch5b.txt`. Inputs: round-1 review `staging/review_supertraining_ch5b_opus.md` and fix log `staging/fixes_supertraining_ch5b_applied.md`. My job was to falsify: check that each round-1 fix landed and is correct, and that no fix added a new error.\n\nSource: `staging/books/supertraining-6th-expanded.pdf`, PDF idx = printed + 11. I extracted the text layer of PDF 233 and 278-299 (`staging/_tmp/r2_5b_text.txt`) and rendered the same pages to `staging/_renders/r2_5b_p<N>.png`, plus page-break crops `r2_5b_p292_crop.png` and `r2_5b_p293_crop.png`. **Opened as images:** PDF 281, 282, 284, 285, 286, 287, 288, 289, 292 (crop), 293 (crop), 296, 297, 299. **Text layer only:** PDF 233, 277-278 (5.2.3 link), 280, 283, 293-294 (squat rule). I also checked every quoted string in the 30 files against the text layer by script, with fuzzy matching for OCR noise. Every miss was OCR noise, a figure label (checked on the image) or a non-source quote (baseline, Inference).\n\nSummary: **28 GO, 2 FIX, 0 NO-GO.** All 13 round-1 FIX items and the Wilson note landed and are correct against the pages. One fix added a new wording error (475-jumps, \"untested\"). One round-1 GO entry (weekly frequency) cites baseline line 105 as Eric's \"stated rule\" without the tag that the fixer added to the same line elsewhere.\n\n## Entry table\n\n| File | Verdict | Problem / what I checked | Exact correction |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| claim--high-volume-plyometrics-do-not-build-rebound-fatigue-resistance | GO | Fix 1 landed: `confidence: supported`; the conflict block is now one sentence pointing to brief-max. Both Nicol quotes checked on the images of PDF 280 and PDF 288-289. Line 122 quote is exact and tagged Explicit. Nothing new is wrong. | None. |\n| heuristic--plyometric-surface-footwear-and-simple-apparatus | GO | Fix 2 landed: `supported`, and the different-aims Inference is labelled. On the PDF 289 image the \"as alluded to earlier ... soft-soled shoes and very resilient jumping surfaces\" sentence sits right before the sand finding (Montagni & Cardinale, 1996, 5 days). Swing (rope length sets oscillation time) and Pogo-Stick (\"height of rebound\") match PDF 289. Footwear sentence matches the PDF 284 image. \"suitably firm shock-absorbing surfaces\" matches the PDF 288 image. | None. |\n| heuristic--strength-endurance-load-tempo-and-the-75-80-percent-ceiling | GO | Fix 3 landed. On the PDF 297 image: skaters \"80-85% of 1RM\", 4-12 reps to complete fatigue, 2-4 min (Mikhailov & Panov, 1975); rowers \"50-80%\" (Ulrich et al, 1966). The new specificity quote matches the PDF 296 image (\"carry-over\" is hyphenated across a line break). The 8 determinants, 25-50%, 60-120/min, 60% and the 75-80% ceiling (Zatsiorsky, 1966) are on PDF 296. Baseline quotes: line 116 \"worst case scenario\" (Explicit) and line 117 \"staff do program it in the off-season\" (Explicit, Q19) are exact. | None. |\n| heuristic--brief-maximal-tension-vs-plyometrics-by-resistance-size | GO | Fix 4 landed. (1) The line 76 tag is verbatim: \"[contested; the ratio tracks IMTP strength; one controlled trial (Pleša 2024, basketball, split at 0.90) supported only the strength arm; no football data]\". The Q21 quote is exact. The \"Tension 17 ... (line 261)\" pointer is correct; line 261 is Tension 17. (2) The Example now quotes PDF 289 and no longer says \"jumping from depth\". (3) The novice caveat matches the PDF 299 image: within-workout experiment, \"pauses ... increased slightly\", \"There was no statistically significant difference\", largest increase \"in the third group\" (depth jumps). The across-stage experiment (\"the first variant was more effective\") and \"the validity of this hypothesis can be established conclusively only by careful experimentation\" are also there. The 40% / 30% / 80% figures and both contested sentences check on the PDF 288-289 images. | None. |\n| claim--depth-jump-training-beat-higher-volume-traditional-training-in-jumpers | **FIX** | Fix 5 landed: the title says \"93 Tons\" and the 5c link is added. The numbers check on the PDF 288 image (475 jumps, 12 weeks, 1472 push-offs, 90-95% / 70-80% / 30-40%, 93 tons). **New error added by the fix:** When NOT says \"The resistance-first rule is untested for novices:\", then cites the PDF 299 experiment, which tested it on novices and found \"no statistically significant difference\". The sentence contradicts itself, and the brief-max entry, fixed in the same round, correctly says \"not supported for novices\". (Round 1 suggested \"untested\"; the fixer followed it.) | Replace \"The resistance-first rule is untested for novices:\" with \"The resistance-first rule is not supported for novices:\". |\n| heuristic--depth-jump-height-set-by-transition-speed-and-heel-contact | GO | Fix 6 landed. The line 74 quote \"was deliberately chosen as the daily athlete-readiness marker\" is exact and tagged Explicit; the drop-jump RSI idea is labelled Inference. \"using considerably lower jump heights with anyone who is unused to this type of training\" is on PDF 233 (text layer; 233 - 11 = printed 222, locator correct). Items 1, 5 and 8 and the \"strength fitness\" sentence check on the images of PDF 285-287. The Fig 5.10 description matches the PDF 286 image (\"Horizontal Projection\" over two variants, \"Vertical Projection\" with a hanging marker). | None. |\n| heuristic--maximal-plyometric-and-depth-jump-volume-and-rest | GO | Fix 7 landed. Item 1 is out of Model 2 and labelled Inference. The PDF 286 image prints \"1-15 minutes\". The PDF 287 image shows Fig 5.11 with no box: vertical, tuck, split and reach-to-marker jumps. Voices are labelled per item, which the page supports. Item 2 (4×10, 2-3×5-8, 10-15 min easy running), item 3 (3×/week, 2×10), item 4 (5-8 reps) and item 6 (~10 min) check on the PDF 285-286 images. Model 1 (2-4 min, 10-12 min) checks on PDF 283 (text layer). \"over 100\" checks on PDF 293. Baseline: the line 105 quote is exact, with tag \"Inferred (transcript + shared slides)\" and \"Not claimed in the interview\"; the line 186 quote is exact with tag Explicit (Q15). | Optional: after the 72-hour Inference, add \"the book's own in-season limit is stricter: no depth jumps within 10 days of competition (item 5, PDF 286; see [[heuristic--depth-jump-weekly-frequency-and-seasonal-placement]])\". The Inference is labelled and true, but a reader could take 72 h as the operative rule. |\n| framework--five-phases-of-a-plyometric-action | GO | Fix 8 landed: \"The caption words the EM delay differently\", then both quotes, then \"Inference: both describe the electrical-to-mechanical interval\"; \"does not reconcile\" is gone. Caption and item 2 match the PDF 281 image. The Fig 5.5 description (boxes, EM delay, eccentric and concentric bars, \"Explosive Isometrics / Coupling Time\") matches. | None. |\n| framework--plyometric-training-classification-impact-intensity-and-function | GO | Fix 9 landed: no \"the authors\" left; voice is Siff, using \"powermetrics\". The Fig 5.8 description matches the PDF 284 image box for box, including \"Preparatory/Supplementary Activities\" over \"Weight Training\" and \"Jumps Throws Etc\". The new F = ma paragraph is verbatim on the PDF 284 image. The note that no study is given is correct. The [[principle--equal-force-different-loading-methods]] link resolves. | None. |\n| heuristic--rate-plyometric-intensity-by-contact-momentum-from-drop-height | GO | Fix 9 landed: Siff voice for the PDF 283 scale, \"the authors'\" for items 1 and 4. Items 1 and 4 match the PDF 285 image. The new Fig 5.9 paragraph matches the PDF 285 image: caption exact; drop push-ups between blocks; pulley and weight-stack pushes, pulls, squat pull, kicks, overhead pull, seated row; incline-board work; seated kick at a suspended object beside a wall pad. It is marked approximate. The weight-stack free-fall reading is labelled Inference. Physics re-checked: m√(2gh) at 100 kg is 313 and 443 kg·m/s, ratio √2. | None. |\n| claim--lewis-formula-estimates-jump-power-from-bodymass-and-height | GO | Fix 10 landed: the Inference in the title is labelled; line 77 carries its verbatim tag \"Inferred (protocol; author uncertain)\" (disagreement 5 justified). Formula \"(21.693) B√H\" matches the PDF 288 image. 21.693 = 9.8 × √4.9 re-checked. | None. |\n| claim--plyometric-injury-risk-comes-from-prescription-not-the-method | GO | Fix 11 landed. The PDF 281 image shows the right-margin cut: \"adequ\", \"running a\", \"te\", \"wi\". The bracketed restorations are marked. The new \"drills ... militarism\" bullet matches the image and is labelled Siff. On PDF 280 (text layer): \"Siff's former colleague, Dr Mark Swanepoel, at the University of the Witwatersrand\", the five cartilage cites and Swanepoel 1998. | None. |\n| heuristic--resisted-and-water-plyometrics | GO | Fix 12 landed. The crops show \"No resistance\" at the foot of PDF 292 and \"methods should not use heavy weights or stiff elastic cords during depth jumps\" at the head of PDF 293. The (sic) note and the Inference label are correct. The aqua sentences match the PDF 293 image. | None. |\n| claim--prestretch-benefit-decay-time-differs-by-task | GO | The Wilson source note is correct (see the Wilson section below). On the PDF 281 image the text gives \"Wilson et al (1990) ... 4 seconds\". PDF 282 gives Chapman & Caldwell 0.25 s, \"Wilson et al (1991) ... 0.37 second\" and the Fig 5.6 caption \"based on the data of Wilson et al, 1991\". Fig 5.6 readings agree with the image: about 50% near 0.8-1 s, about 80% at 2 s, near 100% at about 4 s. Fig 5.7 is near-linear over 0.1-0.25 s. `contested` is kept and is justified (\"apparent contradiction\", PDF 282). | None. |\n| heuristic--depth-jump-weekly-frequency-and-seasonal-placement | **FIX** | Spot check: items 3, 4 and 5 match the PDF 286 image (once or twice a week; 3×/week, 2×10; 3-4 days; 10-14 days; 10 days). Item 15 (5-6 days) matches the PDF 287 image. **Problem:** \"Eric's baseline: 'In-season, the stated rule is \"maintain intensity, reduce volume\"' (`docs/method-baseline.md` line 105)\" has no tag. Line 105 is **Inferred (transcript + shared slides)**, and the baseline adds \"Not claimed in the interview\". With no tag, an inferred, unclaimed line reads as Eric's stated rule, which is the attribution failure this gate exists to catch. The fixer tagged the same quote in the volume-and-rest entry. | After \"(`docs/method-baseline.md` line 105\" insert \", Inferred (transcript + shared slides); the baseline adds \\\"Not claimed in the interview\\\"\". Optional, from round 1: also cite line 186 (Explicit, Q15: \"lifting and hard practice end 72 hours before a Saturday game\"). |\n| case-study--soviet-sport-specific-strength-endurance-prescriptions | GO | Spot check on the PDF 297 image: Chistyakov 65%; Likachyevskaya & Kovalchuk 55-60% bodymass, 8-10 times, 60-85%, one-third bodymass for 18-20 reps, squats 55-60% to fatigue; Popov 60-80%; skaters 80-85%, 4-12 reps, 2-4 min, 15-25 reps, 3-5 sets, 5-8 min; rowers 50-80% and 30-40%; Chumakova 18-20 kg, 40%, 35-50 kg, 2-3 reps, 28%; squats +20-30 a week, from 50 to 200-300 reps over 2-3 months. All match. | None. |\n| claim--zatsiorsky-and-hansen-show-strength-endurance-training-specificity | GO | Spot check on the PDF 296 image: 84%, 10 times a day, 5 weeks, 60%, 93%, \"28 repetitions per minute\" (faint first digit, reads 28), 5 s tension and 2 s rest, 219%. The Hansen 1963 sentence runs onto PDF 297 (image). All match. | None. |\n| claim--depth-landings-from-2-to-3-2-m-produce-forces-over-20-times-bodyweight | GO | Spot check on the PDF 288 image: Dursenev and Raevsky (1978), \"2m or more\", \"soft gymnastic mats\", 0.028-0.061 secs, 1500-3500 kgf, \"over 20 times bodyweight\", \"up to 3.2 metres\", the inadvisable-3.2 m caveat, \"limit the number of drops per session\", \"suitably firm shock-absorbing surfaces\". All match. | Optional, from round 1, still open: \"holds for a 75 kg subject\" would read better as \"needs a bodymass under 75 kg at 1500 kgf\". |\n| heuristic--preparatory-progression-before-depth-jumps | GO | Spot check on the PDF 286-288 images: item 1 \"several months\" and the contra-indications; item 6 \"about 25 repetitions\" then \"about 20\"; item 7 skipping; items 13-14; the eccentric and explosive-isometric bullet; front and back squats; static start; upper-body transfer on PDF 288. Line 101 quotes (\"each level a required foundation for the next\", \"compass\") are exact. | None. Optional consistency: add the line 101 tag \"Explicit (interview 2026-09-28, Q1)\". |\n| claim--squat-1-5-to-2-bodymass-rule-applies-to-maximal-depth-jumps-only | GO | Spot check on the PDF 293 text layer: \"squat 1.5-2 times bodymass\", \"rightly criticize\", \"can easily exceed 6 times bodyweight\", \"never intended to apply religiously to submaximal plyometrics\". All match. | None. |\n| heuristic--depth-jump-execution-cues-landing-gaze-breath | GO | Partial spot check on the images of PDF 284-287: landing \"slightly flexed ... balls of the feet\", item 2 posture, item 3 warm-up, item 9 gaze, item 10 \"falling in a relaxed state\", item 12 breath held, and \"Forced exhalation\" on PDF 284. All match. | None. |\n| claim--heavy-squats-and-light-fast-lifts-miss-the-eccentric-concentric-switch | GO | Round-1 GO stands. Not re-checked against page images in round 2. Its quotes match the text layer (OCR-level), and the line 104 quote is exact. | Optional consistency: add the line 104 tag \"Inferred (transcript + slides)\". |\n| claim--popular-plyometric-drills-work-through-other-mechanisms | GO | Round-1 GO stands. The PDF 293 part was checked on the crop image (Chu 1992; Radcliffe & Farantinos 1985; medicine-ball sentence). Quotes match the text layer. | Optional, from round 1: \"p. 294 from the text layer\" to \"verified\" (round 1 opened it). |\n| claim--strength-endurance-hypertrophy-and-cyclic-endurance | GO | Round-1 GO stands. Maisuradze 25%, Maison & Broeker, McMorris & Elkins, R = 0.77 (Zhalei 1964) seen on the PDF 297 image. The Ch4 quote is outside the extracted range and was not re-checked. | None. |\n| claim--plyometric-skill-is-cognitive-and-state-dependent | GO | Round-1 GO stands. Quotes match the PDF 294-295 text layer (OCR-level). Not re-checked against page images in round 2. | None. |\n| framework--non-impact-plyometrics-ericson-and-martial-arts | GO | Round-1 GO stands. The 1994 NSCA sentence and the martial-arts list were seen on the PDF 292 crop. Quotes match the text layer. | None. |\n| framework--shock-methods-to-break-training-stagnation | GO | Round-1 GO stands. The 8 methods and the caution sentence were seen on the PDF 296 image. | None. |\n| heuristic--plyometric-training-coupling-under-0-15-s-feedforward-and-force-time-pattern | GO | Round-1 GO stands. Quotes match the text layer. The line 96 quote is exact. | Optional consistency: add the line 96 tag \"Inferred (transcript)\". |\n| heuristic--match-plyometric-drills-to-limb-symmetry-and-rotational-dominance | GO | Round-1 GO stands. The asymmetric-plyometrics opening was seen on the PDF 289 image. Quotes match the text layer. | None. |\n| heuristic--strength-endurance-under-demanding-sport-like-conditions | GO | Round-1 GO stands. Popov 1966, Zhilei 1964, Chuprun 1966, 57.1%, 27.8% and 9.1% were seen on the PDF 297 image. The 5.2.3 quote (\"good results are achieved by making the special exercise more demanding\", \"water resistance in rowing ...\") was checked on the PDF 277-278 text layer. | None. |\n\n## Wilson source note (prestretch entry)\n\n- **The reference exists.** PubMed PMID 2020276: Wilson GJ, Elliott BC, Wood GA. \"The effect on performance of imposing a delay during a stretch-shorten cycle movement.\" *Med Sci Sports Exerc*. 1991 Mar;23(3):364-70. I pulled it through NCBI E-utilities, not the fixer's route.\n- **The entry claims no more than the abstract supports.** The abstract gives twelve experienced male weight lifters, bench press at 95% of maximum, pause periods imposed between the downward and upward phases, and decay \"accurately described ... by a negative exponential equation with a half-life of 0.85 s.\" It gives no 4 s figure and no 0.37 s figure. The entry says each of these.\n- **The Fig 5.6 match is labelled.** \"Inference: the 0.85 s half-life matches the Fig 5.6 curve ... probably the bench-press study ... would make the caption's 1991 right and the text's '1990' wrong.\" On the image the curve crosses 50% at roughly 0.8-1 s, so the Inference holds. One more check: an exponential with a 0.85 s half-life is about 96% decayed at 4 s, which fits the near-100% at about 4 s in the figure.\n- **Nothing is overstated.** The note says the 0.37 s Wilson (1991) result was not checked, and it leaves `contested` in place on the book's own \"apparent contradiction\".\n\n## Confidence changes\n\n| Entry | Change | Justified by the page? |\n|---|---|---|\n| high-volume-plyometrics | contested to supported | Yes. The Nicol (1997) claim is stated the same way twice (PDF 280; PDF 288). The \"futile ... predominantly\" vs \"main method\" clash (PDF 289) is about explosive strength, not fatigue resistance, and is kept in brief-max. One undescribed citation fits `supported`. |\n| surface-footwear | contested to supported | Yes. On PDF 289 the sand finding opens with \"as alluded to earlier ... soft-soled shoes and very resilient jumping surfaces\", so the author places the two side by side on purpose. The mats belong to a no-rebound landing study (PDF 288). No other library source is cited against it. |\n| 75-80% ceiling | conflict narrowed to skaters | Yes. On PDF 297 the skaters' 80-85% is above the ceiling, and the rowers' 50-80% reaches only its edge. `contested` stays on the skater conflict alone, which is real. |\n\n## Fixer disagreements\n\n1. **Upper-body transfer is already captured.** Justified. `heuristic--preparatory-progression-before-depth-jumps.md` line 23 holds the PDF 288 medicine-ball, press-up and bench-press sentence.\n2. **The novice caveat is scoped to the within-workout experiment.** Justified. PDF 299 has three findings: order \"has no real significance for novices\" across the preparatory period; the across-stage weights-then-depth-jumps variant \"was more effective\"; and the within-workout test found \"no statistically significant difference\". The fixer's wording is more accurate than round 1's. The one slip is the leftover word \"untested\" in the 475 entry (FIX above).\n3. **Item 1 is read as ground jumps by Inference, not fact.** Justified. \"Each exercise\" can grammatically take in the depth jumps, and Fig 5.11 shows no box.\n4. **Voice is labelled per item, not per model.** Justified. Items 4 and 6 sit in the PDF 285 prescription list. The PDF 286 list says \"Prolific experience\" and carries no citation; only its figures are credited to Verkhoshansky (1977).\n5. **The full line 77 tag is used.** Justified; it is verbatim.\n6. **Tags were added to every baseline citation in the edited files.** Every tag checked against method-baseline.md: 74 Explicit, 76 Explicit (Q21) plus its bracket tag, 77 Inferred (protocol; author uncertain), 105 Inferred (transcript + shared slides), 116 Explicit, 117 Explicit (Q19), 122 Explicit, 186 Explicit (Q15). All exact. The fixer did not extend this to the unedited files, which is why the weekly-frequency row is FIX.\n7. **Round-1 optional items for GO files were not applied.** Acceptable under the flagged-files-only rule. The line 105 tag in weekly frequency was more than cosmetic, so it is raised to FIX here.\n\n## Mechanical checks (all 30 files)\n\n- Wikilinks: 160 checked, all resolve in the staging library or the vault. None is wrapped across lines.\n- Section headers: all 30 files have each of the six headers exactly once, in the `**X** —` form.\n- Em dashes outside headers: 0. Titles: 0.\n- Review-history wording: 0. A keyword scan flagged 5 lines; all are ordinary prose (\"fixed function\", \"a corrected value\", \"not fixed by drop height\").\n- CR line endings: 0.\n\n## For the coordinator (outside scope, not a verdict item)\n\n- `case-study--novice-strength-and-speed-strength-sequencing-experiments.md` (5c) already links back to the 475-jumps entry. It does not link to `heuristic--brief-maximal-tension-vs-plyometrics-by-resistance-size`, which now cites it. Add that reciprocal link.\n\n## Overall verdict\n\n**GO AFTER FIXES.** Two one-line fixes:\n1. `claim--depth-jump-training-beat-higher-volume-traditional-training-in-jumpers.md`: change \"untested for novices\" to \"not supported for novices\".\n2. `heuristic--depth-jump-weekly-frequency-and-seasonal-placement.md`: tag the line 105 citation \"Inferred (transcript + shared slides); the baseline adds \\\"Not claimed in the interview\\\"\".\n\nAfter those two, the batch is ready to promote. Neither needs another full review round; a grep confirming both strings is enough.\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":5,"requestId":"req_011Cffd2fLKzU2RrcpxSEqap","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"2dc92635-7c69-4af4-986b-a948de5fcd45","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:33:39.368Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
{"parentUuid":"2dc92635-7c69-4af4-986b-a948de5fcd45","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb365d2b-3f81-4d84-a7bf-7472b0a309d6","agentId":"ac44742970c7341bd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YVxukNj4oFTT7g6eQ3DJpr","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch5b_opus_round2.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"012701e3-2892-4fb0-b6df-4faf65d3df7f","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:33:39.499Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch5b_opus_round2.md","content":"# Review round 2: Supertraining Ch 5 batch 5b (5.2.4-5.2.5), Opus independent reviewer\n\nScope: the 30 files in `staging/_scope_supertraining_ch5b.txt`. Inputs: round-1 review `staging/review_supertraining_ch5b_opus.md` and fix log `staging/fixes_supertraining_ch5b_applied.md`. My job was to falsify: check that each round-1 fix landed and is correct, and that no fix added a new error.\n\nSource: `staging/books/supertraining-6th-expanded.pdf`, PDF idx = printed + 11. I extracted the text layer of PDF 233 and 278-299 (`staging/_tmp/r2_5b_text.txt`) and rendered the same pages to `staging/_renders/r2_5b_p<N>.png`, plus page-break crops `r2_5b_p292_crop.png` and `r2_5b_p293_crop.png`. **Opened as images:** PDF 281, 282, 284, 285, 286, 287, 288, 289, 292 (crop), 293 (crop), 296, 297, 299. **Text layer only:** PDF 233, 277-278 (5.2.3 link), 280, 283, 293-294 (squat rule). I also checked every quoted string in the 30 files against the text layer by script, with fuzzy matching for OCR noise. Every miss was OCR noise, a figure label (checked on the image) or a non-source quote (baseline, Inference).\n\nSummary: **28 GO, 2 FIX, 0 NO-GO.** All 13 round-1 FIX items and the Wilson note landed and are correct against the pages. One fix added a new wording error (475-jumps, \"untested\"). One round-1 GO entry (weekly frequency) cites baseline line 105 as Eric's \"stated rule\" without the tag that the fixer added to the same line elsewhere.\n\n## Entry table\n\n| File | Verdict | Problem / what I checked | Exact correction |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| claim--high-volume-plyometrics-do-not-build-rebound-fatigue-resistance | GO | Fix 1 landed: `confidence: supported`; the conflict block is now one sentence pointing to brief-max. Both Nicol quotes checked on the images of PDF 280 and PDF 288-289. Line 122 quote is exact and tagged Explicit. Nothing new is wrong. | None. |\n| heuristic--plyometric-surface-footwear-and-simple-apparatus | GO | Fix 2 landed: `supported`, and the different-aims Inference is labelled. On the PDF 289 image the \"as alluded to earlier ... soft-soled shoes and very resilient jumping surfaces\" sentence sits right before the sand finding (Montagni & Cardinale, 1996, 5 days). Swing (rope length sets oscillation time) and Pogo-Stick (\"height of rebound\") match PDF 289. Footwear sentence matches the PDF 284 image. \"suitably firm shock-absorbing surfaces\" matches the PDF 288 image. | None. |\n| heuristic--strength-endurance-load-tempo-and-the-75-80-percent-ceiling | GO | Fix 3 landed. On the PDF 297 image: skaters \"80-85% of 1RM\", 4-12 reps to complete fatigue, 2-4 min (Mikhailov & Panov, 1975); rowers \"50-80%\" (Ulrich et al, 1966). The new specificity quote matches the PDF 296 image (\"carry-over\" is hyphenated across a line break). The 8 determinants, 25-50%, 60-120/min, 60% and the 75-80% ceiling (Zatsiorsky, 1966) are on PDF 296. Baseline quotes: line 116 \"worst case scenario\" (Explicit) and line 117 \"staff do program it in the off-season\" (Explicit, Q19) are exact. | None. |\n| heuristic--brief-maximal-tension-vs-plyometrics-by-resistance-size | GO | Fix 4 landed. (1) The line 76 tag is verbatim: \"[contested; the ratio tracks IMTP strength; one controlled trial (Pleša 2024, basketball, split at 0.90) supported only the strength arm; no football data]\". The Q21 quote is exact. The \"Tension 17 ... (line 261)\" pointer is correct; line 261 is Tension 17. (2) The Example now quotes PDF 289 and no longer says \"jumping from depth\". (3) The novice caveat matches the PDF 299 image: within-workout experiment, \"pauses ... increased slightly\", \"There was no statistically significant difference\", largest increase \"in the third group\" (depth jumps). The across-stage experiment (\"the first variant was more effective\") and \"the validity of this hypothesis can be established conclusively only by careful experimentation\" are also there. The 40% / 30% / 80% figures and both contested sentences check on the PDF 288-289 images. | None. |\n| claim--depth-jump-training-beat-higher-volume-traditional-training-in-jumpers | **FIX** | Fix 5 landed: the title says \"93 Tons\" and the 5c link is added. The numbers check on the PDF 288 image (475 jumps, 12 weeks, 1472 push-offs, 90-95% / 70-80% / 30-40%, 93 tons). **New error added by the fix:** When NOT says \"The resistance-first rule is untested for novices:\", then cites the PDF 299 experiment, which tested it on novices and found \"no statistically significant difference\". The sentence contradicts itself, and the brief-max entry, fixed in the same round, correctly says \"not supported for novices\". (Round 1 suggested \"untested\"; the fixer followed it.) | Replace \"The resistance-first rule is untested for novices:\" with \"The resistance-first rule is not supported for novices:\". |\n| heuristic--depth-jump-height-set-by-transition-speed-and-heel-contact | GO | Fix 6 landed. The line 74 quote \"was deliberately chosen as the daily athlete-readiness marker\" is exact and tagged Explicit; the drop-jump RSI idea is labelled Inference. \"using considerably lower jump heights with anyone who is unused to this type of training\" is on PDF 233 (text layer; 233 - 11 = printed 222, locator correct). Items 1, 5 and 8 and the \"strength fitness\" sentence check on the images of PDF 285-287. The Fig 5.10 description matches the PDF 286 image (\"Horizontal Projection\" over two variants, \"Vertical Projection\" with a hanging marker). | None. |\n| heuristic--maximal-plyometric-and-depth-jump-volume-and-rest | GO | Fix 7 landed. Item 1 is out of Model 2 and labelled Inference. The PDF 286 image prints \"1-15 minutes\". The PDF 287 image shows Fig 5.11 with no box: vertical, tuck, split and reach-to-marker jumps. Voices are labelled per item, which the page supports. Item 2 (4×10, 2-3×5-8, 10-15 min easy running), item 3 (3×/week, 2×10), item 4 (5-8 reps) and item 6 (~10 min) check on the PDF 285-286 images. Model 1 (2-4 min, 10-12 min) checks on PDF 283 (text layer). \"over 100\" checks on PDF 293. Baseline: the line 105 quote is exact, with tag \"Inferred (transcript + shared slides)\" and \"Not claimed in the interview\"; the line 186 quote is exact with tag Explicit (Q15). | Optional: after the 72-hour Inference, add \"the book's own in-season limit is stricter: no depth jumps within 10 days of competition (item 5, PDF 286; see [[heuristic--depth-jump-weekly-frequency-and-seasonal-placement]])\". The Inference is labelled and true, but a reader could take 72 h as the operative rule. |\n| framework--five-phases-of-a-plyometric-action | GO | Fix 8 landed: \"The caption words the EM delay differently\", then both quotes, then \"Inference: both describe the electrical-to-mechanical interval\"; \"does not reconcile\" is gone. Caption and item 2 match the PDF 281 image. The Fig 5.5 description (boxes, EM delay, eccentric and concentric bars, \"Explosive Isometrics / Coupling Time\") matches. | None. |\n| framework--plyometric-training-classification-impact-intensity-and-function | GO | Fix 9 landed: no \"the authors\" left; voice is Siff, using \"powermetrics\". The Fig 5.8 description matches the PDF 284 image box for box, including \"Preparatory/Supplementary Activities\" over \"Weight Training\" and \"Jumps Throws Etc\". The new F = ma paragraph is verbatim on the PDF 284 image. The note that no study is given is correct. The [[principle--equal-force-different-loading-methods]] link resolves. | None. |\n| heuristic--rate-plyometric-intensity-by-contact-momentum-from-drop-height | GO | Fix 9 landed: Siff voice for the PDF 283 scale, \"the authors'\" for items 1 and 4. Items 1 and 4 match the PDF 285 image. The new Fig 5.9 paragraph matches the PDF 285 image: caption exact; drop push-ups between blocks; pulley and weight-stack pushes, pulls, squat pull, kicks, overhead pull, seated row; incline-board work; seated kick at a suspended object beside a wall pad. It is marked approximate. The weight-stack free-fall reading is labelled Inference. Physics re-checked: m√(2gh) at 100 kg is 313 and 443 kg·m/s, ratio √2. | None. |\n| claim--lewis-formula-estimates-jump-power-from-bodymass-and-height | GO | Fix 10 landed: the Inference in the title is labelled; line 77 carries its verbatim tag \"Inferred (protocol; author uncertain)\" (disagreement 5 justified). Formula \"(21.693) B√H\" matches the PDF 288 image. 21.693 = 9.8 × √4.9 re-checked. | None. |\n| claim--plyometric-injury-risk-comes-from-prescription-not-the-method | GO | Fix 11 landed. The PDF 281 image shows the right-margin cut: \"adequ\", \"running a\", \"te\", \"wi\". The bracketed restorations are marked. The new \"drills ... militarism\" bullet matches the image and is labelled Siff. On PDF 280 (text layer): \"Siff's former colleague, Dr Mark Swanepoel, at the University of the Witwatersrand\", the five cartilage cites and Swanepoel 1998. | None. |\n| heuristic--resisted-and-water-plyometrics | GO | Fix 12 landed. The crops show \"No resistance\" at the foot of PDF 292 and \"methods should not use heavy weights or stiff elastic cords during depth jumps\" at the head of PDF 293. The (sic) note and the Inference label are correct. The aqua sentences match the PDF 293 image. | None. |\n| claim--prestretch-benefit-decay-time-differs-by-task | GO | The Wilson source note is correct (see the Wilson section below). On the PDF 281 image the text gives \"Wilson et al (1990) ... 4 seconds\". PDF 282 gives Chapman & Caldwell 0.25 s, \"Wilson et al (1991) ... 0.37 second\" and the Fig 5.6 caption \"based on the data of Wilson et al, 1991\". Fig 5.6 readings agree with the image: about 50% near 0.8-1 s, about 80% at 2 s, near 100% at about 4 s. Fig 5.7 is near-linear over 0.1-0.25 s. `contested` is kept and is justified (\"apparent contradiction\", PDF 282). | None. |\n| heuristic--depth-jump-weekly-frequency-and-seasonal-placement | **FIX** | Spot check: items 3, 4 and 5 match the PDF 286 image (once or twice a week; 3×/week, 2×10; 3-4 days; 10-14 days; 10 days). Item 15 (5-6 days) matches the PDF 287 image. **Problem:** \"Eric's baseline: 'In-season, the stated rule is \"maintain intensity, reduce volume\"' (`docs/method-baseline.md` line 105)\" has no tag. Line 105 is **Inferred (transcript + shared slides)**, and the baseline adds \"Not claimed in the interview\". With no tag, an inferred, unclaimed line reads as Eric's stated rule, which is the attribution failure this gate exists to catch. The fixer tagged the same quote in the volume-and-rest entry. | After \"(`docs/method-baseline.md` line 105\" insert \", Inferred (transcript + shared slides); the baseline adds \\\"Not claimed in the interview\\\"\". Optional, from round 1: also cite line 186 (Explicit, Q15: \"lifting and hard practice end 72 hours before a Saturday game\"). |\n| case-study--soviet-sport-specific-strength-endurance-prescriptions | GO | Spot check on the PDF 297 image: Chistyakov 65%; Likachyevskaya & Kovalchuk 55-60% bodymass, 8-10 times, 60-85%, one-third bodymass for 18-20 reps, squats 55-60% to fatigue; Popov 60-80%; skaters 80-85%, 4-12 reps, 2-4 min, 15-25 reps, 3-5 sets, 5-8 min; rowers 50-80% and 30-40%; Chumakova 18-20 kg, 40%, 35-50 kg, 2-3 reps, 28%; squats +20-30 a week, from 50 to 200-300 reps over 2-3 months. All match. | None. |\n| claim--zatsiorsky-and-hansen-show-strength-endurance-training-specificity | GO | Spot check on the PDF 296 image: 84%, 10 times a day, 5 weeks, 60%, 93%, \"28 repetitions per minute\" (faint first digit, reads 28), 5 s tension and 2 s rest, 219%. The Hansen 1963 sentence runs onto PDF 297 (image). All match. | None. |\n| claim--depth-landings-from-2-to-3-2-m-produce-forces-over-20-times-bodyweight | GO | Spot check on the PDF 288 image: Dursenev and Raevsky (1978), \"2m or more\", \"soft gymnastic mats\", 0.028-0.061 secs, 1500-3500 kgf, \"over 20 times bodyweight\", \"up to 3.2 metres\", the inadvisable-3.2 m caveat, \"limit the number of drops per session\", \"suitably firm shock-absorbing surfaces\". All match. | Optional, from round 1, still open: \"holds for a 75 kg subject\" would read better as \"needs a bodymass under 75 kg at 1500 kgf\". |\n| heuristic--preparatory-progression-before-depth-jumps | GO | Spot check on the PDF 286-288 images: item 1 \"several months\" and the contra-indications; item 6 \"about 25 repetitions\" then \"about 20\"; item 7 skipping; items 13-14; the eccentric and explosive-isometric bullet; front and back squats; static start; upper-body transfer on PDF 288. Line 101 quotes (\"each level a required foundation for the next\", \"compass\") are exact. | None. Optional consistency: add the line 101 tag \"Explicit (interview 2026-09-28, Q1)\". |\n| claim--squat-1-5-to-2-bodymass-rule-applies-to-maximal-depth-jumps-only | GO | Spot check on the PDF 293 text layer: \"squat 1.5-2 times bodymass\", \"rightly criticize\", \"can easily exceed 6 times bodyweight\", \"never intended to apply religiously to submaximal plyometrics\". All match. | None. |\n| heuristic--depth-jump-execution-cues-landing-gaze-breath | GO | Partial spot check on the images of PDF 284-287: landing \"slightly flexed ... balls of the feet\", item 2 posture, item 3 warm-up, item 9 gaze, item 10 \"falling in a relaxed state\", item 12 breath held, and \"Forced exhalation\" on PDF 284. All match. | None. |\n| claim--heavy-squats-and-light-fast-lifts-miss-the-eccentric-concentric-switch | GO | Round-1 GO stands. Not re-checked against page images in round 2. Its quotes match the text layer (OCR-level), and the line 104 quote is exact. | Optional consistency: add the line 104 tag \"Inferred (transcript + slides)\". |\n| claim--popular-plyometric-drills-work-through-other-mechanisms | GO | Round-1 GO stands. The PDF 293 part was checked on the crop image (Chu 1992; Radcliffe & Farantinos 1985; medicine-ball sentence). Quotes match the text layer. | Optional, from round 1: \"p. 294 from the text layer\" to \"verified\" (round 1 opened it). |\n| claim--strength-endurance-hypertrophy-and-cyclic-endurance | GO | Round-1 GO stands. Maisuradze 25%, Maison & Broeker, McMorris & Elkins, R = 0.77 (Zhalei 1964) seen on the PDF 297 image. The Ch4 quote is outside the extracted range and was not re-checked. | None. |\n| claim--plyometric-skill-is-cognitive-and-state-dependent | GO | Round-1 GO stands. Quotes match the PDF 294-295 text layer (OCR-level). Not re-checked against page images in round 2. | None. |\n| framework--non-impact-plyometrics-ericson-and-martial-arts | GO | Round-1 GO stands. The 1994 NSCA sentence and the martial-arts list were seen on the PDF 292 crop. Quotes match the text layer. | None. |\n| framework--shock-methods-to-break-training-stagnation | GO | Round-1 GO stands. The 8 methods and the caution sentence were seen on the PDF 296 image. | None. |\n| heuristic--plyometric-training-coupling-under-0-15-s-feedforward-and-force-time-pattern | GO | Round-1 GO stands. Quotes match the text layer. The line 96 quote is exact. | Optional consistency: add the line 96 tag \"Inferred (transcript)\". |\n| heuristic--match-plyometric-drills-to-limb-symmetry-and-rotational-dominance | GO | Round-1 GO stands. The asymmetric-plyometrics opening was seen on the PDF 289 image. Quotes match the text layer. | None. |\n| heuristic--strength-endurance-under-demanding-sport-like-conditions | GO | Round-1 GO stands. Popov 1966, Zhilei 1964, Chuprun 1966, 57.1%, 27.8% and 9.1% were seen on the PDF 297 image. The 5.2.3 quote (\"good results are achieved by making the special exercise more demanding\", \"water resistance in rowing ...\") was checked on the PDF 277-278 text layer. | None. |\n\n## Wilson source note (prestretch entry)\n\n- **The reference exists.** PubMed PMID 2020276: Wilson GJ, Elliott BC, Wood GA. \"The effect on performance of imposing a delay during a stretch-shorten cycle movement.\" *Med Sci Sports Exerc*. 1991 Mar;23(3):364-70. I pulled it through NCBI E-utilities, not the fixer's route.\n- **The entry claims no more than the abstract supports.** The abstract gives twelve experienced male weight lifters, bench press at 95% of maximum, pause periods imposed between the downward and upward phases, and decay \"accurately described ... by a negative exponential equation with a half-life of 0.85 s.\" It gives no 4 s figure and no 0.37 s figure. The entry says each of these.\n- **The Fig 5.6 match is labelled.** \"Inference: the 0.85 s half-life matches the Fig 5.6 curve ... probably the bench-press study ... would make the caption's 1991 right and the text's '1990' wrong.\" On the image the curve crosses 50% at roughly 0.8-1 s, so the Inference holds. One more check: an exponential with a 0.85 s half-life is about 96% decayed at 4 s, which fits the near-100% at about 4 s in the figure.\n- **Nothing is overstated.** The note says the 0.37 s Wilson (1991) result was not checked, and it leaves `contested` in place on the book's own \"apparent contradiction\".\n\n## Confidence changes\n\n| Entry | Change | Justified by the page? |\n|---|---|---|\n| high-volume-plyometrics | contested to supported | Yes. The Nicol (1997) claim is stated the same way twice (PDF 280; PDF 288). The \"futile ... predominantly\" vs \"main method\" clash (PDF 289) is about explosive strength, not fatigue resistance, and is kept in brief-max. One undescribed citation fits `supported`. |\n| surface-footwear | contested to supported | Yes. On PDF 289 the sand finding opens with \"as alluded to earlier ... soft-soled shoes and very resilient jumping surfaces\", so the author places the two side by side on purpose. The mats belong to a no-rebound landing study (PDF 288). No other library source is cited against it. |\n| 75-80% ceiling | conflict narrowed to skaters | Yes. On PDF 297 the skaters' 80-85% is above the ceiling, and the rowers' 50-80% reaches only its edge. `contested` stays on the skater conflict alone, which is real. |\n\n## Fixer disagreements\n\n1. **Upper-body transfer is already captured.** Justified. `heuristic--preparatory-progression-before-depth-jumps.md` line 23 holds the PDF 288 medicine-ball, press-up and bench-press sentence.\n2. **The novice caveat is scoped to the within-workout experiment.** Justified. PDF 299 has three findings: order \"has no real significance for novices\" across the preparatory period; the across-stage weights-then-depth-jumps variant \"was more effective\"; and the within-workout test found \"no statistically significant difference\". The fixer's wording is more accurate than round 1's. The one slip is the leftover word \"untested\" in the 475 entry (FIX above).\n3. **Item 1 is read as ground jumps by Inference, not fact.** Justified. \"Each exercise\" can grammatically take in the depth jumps, and Fig 5.11 shows no box.\n4. **Voice is labelled per item, not per model.** Justified. Items 4 and 6 sit in the PDF 285 prescription list. The PDF 286 list says \"Prolific experience\" and carries no citation; only its figures are credited to Verkhoshansky (1977).\n5. **The full line 77 tag is used.** Justified; it is verbatim.\n6. **Tags were added to every baseline citation in the edited files.** Every tag checked against method-baseline.md: 74 Explicit, 76 Explicit (Q21) plus its bracket tag, 77 Inferred (protocol; author uncertain), 105 Inferred (transcript + shared slides), 116 Explicit, 117 Explicit (Q19), 122 Explicit, 186 Explicit (Q15). All exact. The fixer did not extend this to the unedited files, which is why the weekly-frequency row is FIX.\n7. **Round-1 optional items for GO files were not applied.** Acceptable under the flagged-files-only rule. The line 105 tag in weekly frequency was more than cosmetic, so it is raised to FIX here.\n\n## Mechanical checks (all 30 files)\n\n- Wikilinks: 160 checked, all resolve in the staging library or the vault. None is wrapped across lines.\n- Section headers: all 30 files have each of the six headers exactly once, in the `**X** —` form.\n- Em dashes outside headers: 0. Titles: 0.\n- Review-history wording: 0. A keyword scan flagged 5 lines; all are ordinary prose (\"fixed function\", \"a corrected value\", \"not fixed by drop height\").\n- CR line endings: 0.\n\n## For the coordinator (outside scope, not a verdict item)\n\n- `case-study--novice-strength-and-speed-strength-sequencing-experiments.md` (5c) already links back to the 475-jumps entry. It does not link to `heuristic--brief-maximal-tension-vs-plyometrics-by-resistance-size`, which now cites it. Add that reciprocal link.\n\n## Overall verdict\n\n**GO AFTER FIXES.** Two one-line fixes:\n1. `claim--depth-jump-training-beat-higher-volume-traditional-training-in-jumpers.md`: change \"untested for novices\" to \"not supported for novices\".\n2. `heuristic--depth-jump-weekly-frequency-and-seasonal-placement.md`: tag the line 105 citation \"Inferred (transcript + shared slides); the baseline adds \\\"Not claimed in the interview\\\"\".\n\nAfter those two, the batch is ready to promote. Neither needs another full review round; a grep confirming both strings is enough.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2dc92635-7c69-4af4-986b-a948de5fcd45","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
