{"parentUuid":"ac539c4c-7ac5-432a-b0f0-eee4ff48fb21","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb365d2b-3f81-4d84-a7bf-7472b0a309d6","agentId":"ac44742970c7341bd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011eCC5ofaVGXw279UHb1us9","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch5b_opus_round2.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"846289bf-4611-40ca-a5cc-1f87ba9cd1a6","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:35:02.522Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch5b_opus_round2.md","oldString":"Both Nicol quotes checked on the images of PDF 280 and PDF 288-289.","newString":"Both Nicol quotes checked: PDF 280 (text layer) and the images of PDF 288-289.","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":10,"oldLines":7,"newStart":10,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," | File | Verdict | Problem / what I checked | Exact correction |"," |---|---|---|---|","-| claim--high-volume-plyometrics-do-not-build-rebound-fatigue-resistance | GO | Fix 1 landed: `confidence: supported`; the conflict block is now one sentence pointing to brief-max. Both Nicol quotes checked on the images of PDF 280 and PDF 288-289. Line 122 quote is exact and tagged Explicit. Nothing new is wrong. | None. |","+| claim--high-volume-plyometrics-do-not-build-rebound-fatigue-resistance | GO | Fix 1 landed: `confidence: supported`; the conflict block is now one sentence pointing to brief-max. Both Nicol quotes checked: PDF 280 (text layer) and the images of PDF 288-289. Line 122 quote is exact and tagged Explicit. Nothing new is wrong. | None. |"," | heuristic--plyometric-surface-footwear-and-simple-apparatus | GO | Fix 2 landed: `supported`, and the different-aims Inference is labelled. On the PDF 289 image the \"as alluded to earlier ... soft-soled shoes and very resilient jumping surfaces\" sentence sits right before the sand finding (Montagni & Cardinale, 1996, 5 days). Swing (rope length sets oscillation time) and Pogo-Stick (\"height of rebound\") match PDF 289. Footwear sentence matches the PDF 284 image. \"suitably firm shock-absorbing surfaces\" matches the PDF 288 image. | None. |"," | heuristic--strength-endurance-load-tempo-and-the-75-80-percent-ceiling | GO | Fix 3 landed. On the PDF 297 image: skaters \"80-85% of 1RM\", 4-12 reps to complete fatigue, 2-4 min (Mikhailov & Panov, 1975); rowers \"50-80%\" (Ulrich et al, 1966). The new specificity quote matches the PDF 296 image (\"carry-over\" is hyphenated across a line break). The 8 determinants, 25-50%, 60-120/min, 60% and the 75-80% ceiling (Zatsiorsky, 1966) are on PDF 296. Baseline quotes: line 116 \"worst case scenario\" (Explicit) and line 117 \"staff do program it in the off-season\" (Explicit, Q19) are exact. | None. |"," | heuristic--brief-maximal-tension-vs-plyometrics-by-resistance-size | GO | Fix 4 landed. (1) The line 76 tag is verbatim: \"[contested; the ratio tracks IMTP strength; one controlled trial (Pleša 2024, basketball, split at 0.90) supported only the strength arm; no football data]\". The Q21 quote is exact. The \"Tension 17 ... (line 261)\" pointer is correct; line 261 is Tension 17. (2) The Example now quotes PDF 289 and no longer says \"jumping from depth\". (3) The novice caveat matches the PDF 299 image: within-workout experiment, \"pauses ... increased slightly\", \"There was no statistically significant difference\", largest increase \"in the third group\" (depth jumps). The across-stage experiment (\"the first variant was more effective\") and \"the validity of this hypothesis can be established conclusively only by careful experimentation\" are also there. The 40% / 30% / 80% figures and both contested sentences check on the PDF 288-289 images. | None. |"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ac539c4c-7ac5-432a-b0f0-eee4ff48fb21","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
