nk is added. The numbers check on the PDF 288 image (475 jumps, 12 weeks, 1472 push-offs, 90-95% / 70-80% / 30-40%, 93 tons). **New error added by the fix:** When NOT says \"The resistance-first rule is untested for novices:\", then cites the PDF 299 experiment, which tested it on novices and found \"no statistically significant difference\". The sentence contradicts itself, and the brief-max entry, fixed in the same round, correctly says \"not supported for novices\". (Round 1 suggested \"untested\"; the fixer followed it.) | Replace \"The resistance-first rule is untested for novices:\" with \"The resistance-first rule is not supported for novices:\". |"," | heuristic--depth-jump-height-set-by-transition-speed-and-heel-contact | GO | Fix 6 landed. The line 74 quote \"was deliberately chosen as the daily athlete-readiness marker\" is exact and tagged Explicit; the drop-jump RSI idea is labelled Inference. \"using considerably lower jump heights with anyone who is unused to this type of training\" is on PDF 233 (text layer; 233 - 11 = printed 222, locator correct). Items 1, 5 and 8 and the \"strength fitness\" sentence check on the images of PDF 285-287. The Fig 5.10 description matches the PDF 286 image (\"Horizontal Projection\" over two variants, \"Vertical Projection\" with a hanging marker). | None. |","-| heuristic--maximal-plyometric-and-depth-jump-volume-and-rest | GO | Fix 7 landed. Item 1 is out of Model 2 and labelled Inference. The PDF 286 image prints \"1-15 minutes\". The PDF 287 image shows Fig 5.11 with no box: vertical, tuck, split and reach-to-marker jumps. Voices are labelled per item, which the page supports. Item 2 (4×10, 2-3×5-8, 10-15 min easy running), item 3 (3×/week, 2×10), item 4 (5-8 reps) and item 6 (~10 min) check on the PDF 285-286 images. Model 1 (2-4 min, 10-12 min) checks on PDF 283 (text layer). \"over 100\" checks on PDF 293. Baseline: the line 105 quote is exact, with tag \"Inferred (transcript + shared slides)\" and \"Not claimed in the interview\"; the line 186 quote is exact with tag Explicit (Q15). | Optional: after the 72-hour Inference, add \"the book's own in-season limit is stricter: no depth jumps within 10 days of competition (item 5, PDF 286; see [[heuristic--depth-jump-weekly-frequency-and-seasonal-placement]])\". The Inference is labelled and true, but a reader could take 72 h as the operative rule. |","+| heuristic--maximal-plyometric-and-depth-jump-volume-and-rest | GO | Fix 7 landed. Item 1 is out of Model 2 and labelled Inference. The PDF 286 image prints \"1-15 minutes\". The PDF 287 image shows Fig 5.11 with no box: vertical, tuck, split and reach-to-marker jumps. Voices are labelled per item, which the page supports. Item 2 (4×10, 2-3×5-8, 10-15 min easy running), item 3 (3×/week, 2×10), item 4 (5-8 reps) and item 6 (~10 min) check on the PDF 285-286 images. Model 1 (2-4 min, 10-12 min) checks on PDF 283 (text layer). \"over 100\" checks on PDF 293 (text layer). Baseline: the line 105 quote is exact, with tag \"Inferred (transcript + shared slides)\" and \"Not claimed in the interview\"; the line 186 quote is exact with tag Explicit (Q15). | Optional: after the 72-hour Inference, add \"the book's own in-season limit is stricter: no depth jumps within 10 days of competition (item 5, PDF 286; see [[heuristic--depth-jump-weekly-frequency-and-seasonal-placement]])\". The Inference is labelled and true, but a reader could take 72 h as the operative rule. |"," | framework--five-phases-of-a-plyometric-action | GO | Fix 8 landed: \"The caption words the EM delay differently\", then both quotes, then \"Inference: both describe the electrical-to-mechanical interval\"; \"does not reconcile\" is gone. Caption and item 2 match the PDF 281 image. The Fig 5.5 description (boxes, EM delay, eccentric and concentric bars, \"Explosive Isometrics / Coupling Time\") matches. | None. |"," | framework--plyometric-training-classification-impact-intensity-and-function | GO | Fix 9 landed: no \"the authors\" left; voice is Siff, using \"powermetrics\". The Fig 5.8 description matches the PDF 284 image box for box, including \"Preparatory/Supplementary Activities\" over \"Weight Training\" and \"Jumps Throws Etc\". The new F = ma paragraph is verbatim on the PDF 284 image. The note that no study is given is correct. The [[principle--equal-force-different-loading-methods]] link resolves. | None. |"," | heuristic--rate-plyometric-intensity-by-contact-momentum-from-drop-height | GO | Fix 9 landed: Siff voice for the PDF 283 scale, \"the authors'\" for items 1 and 4. Items 1 and 4 match the PDF 285 image. The new Fig 5.9 paragraph matches the PDF 285 image: caption exact; drop push-ups between blocks; pulley and weight-stack pushes, pulls, squat pull, kicks, overhead pull, seated row; incline-board work; seated kick at a suspended object beside a wall pad. It is marked approximate. The weight-stack free-fall reading is labelled Inference. Physics re-checked: m√(2gh) at 100 kg is 313 and 443 kg·m/s, ratio √2. | None. |"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e4382742-03ec-4e2c-99c4-6766751aef22","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
