{"parentUuid":"9c965870-c996-4623-8387-3c94314cd26c","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ac44742970c7341bd","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CffdPGWV7RswRz3XR2KUW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Verdict: GO AFTER FIXES.** 28 GO, 2 FIX, 0 NO-GO. Report: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch5b_opus_round2.md`\n\nAll 13 round-1 fixes and the Wilson note are in the files and correct against the page images. Two small fixes are needed:\n\n1. **`claim--depth-jump-training-beat-higher-volume-traditional-training-in-jumpers.md`** (the 475-jumps entry): the fix added a self-contradiction. The entry says the resistance-first rule is \"untested for novices\", then cites the PDF 299 experiment that tested it on novices and found \"no statistically significant difference\". Change \"untested\" to \"not supported\", which is what the brief-max entry already says. Round 1 suggested the \"untested\" wording, and the fixer followed it.\n2. **`heuristic--depth-jump-weekly-frequency-and-seasonal-placement.md`** (a round-1 GO): it quotes `method-baseline.md` line 105 as Eric's \"stated rule\" with no tag. Line 105 is \"Inferred (transcript + shared slides)\" and the baseline adds \"Not claimed in the interview\". Add that tag; the fixer already added it to the same quote in the volume-and-rest entry.\n\nNeither needs another full review round. A grep confirming both strings is enough.\n\n**Other checks:**\n- **Baseline quotes:** every quote is exact, and every tag in the 14 edited files matches the baseline (lines 74, 76, 77, 105, 116, 117, 122, 186). Line 76 carries its bracket tag word for word, and the \"Tension 17 (line 261)\" pointer is correct.\n- **Wilson note:** I confirmed the reference myself through PubMed (PMID 2020276): Wilson, Elliott & Wood, Med Sci Sports Exerc 1991;23(3):364-370. The entry's claims match the abstract: 12 experienced male weight lifters, bench press at 95%, decay fitted by a negative exponential with a 0.85 s half-life, and no 4 s figure. The Fig 5.6 match is labelled Inference, and the figure itself is about 50% decayed near 0.8-1 s.\n- **Confidence changes:** all three hold on the pages.\n  - High-volume, contested to supported: the Nicol claim appears twice (PDF 280, 288) and nothing in the book contradicts it.\n  - Surface-footwear, contested to supported: on PDF 289 the author deliberately places the sand finding next to the soft-surface warning.\n  - Ceiling, narrowed: the skaters' 80-85% is above it; the rowers' 50-80% only reaches its edge.\n- **Fixer disagreements:** all seven are justified by the pages.\n- **Format, all 30 files:** 160 wikilinks all resolve, none wrapped. All six headers in every file. No em dashes outside headers, no review-history wording, no CR line endings.\n\n**GO entries I spot-checked against the pages:** the Soviet strength-endurance case study (PDF 297), Zatsiorsky and Hansen (PDF 296-297), depth landings (PDF 288), preparatory progression (PDF 286-288), the squat 1.5-2 rule (PDF 293, text layer only), weekly frequency (PDF 286-287), and part of the depth-jump execution cues (PDF 284-287). All prescription numbers matched. The other round-1 GO entries passed the scripted quote match and format checks but I did not reopen their page images.\n\n**Optional, not blocking:**\n- In the volume-and-rest entry, the new 72-hour Inference could point out that the book's own in-season limit is stricter: no depth jumps within 10 days of competition (PDF 286).\n- For consistency, the GO entries citing baseline lines 96, 101 and 104 could carry their tags too.\n\n**For the coordinator:** the 5c entry `case-study--novice-strength-and-speed-strength-sequencing-experiments.md` links back to the 475-jumps entry but not to `heuristic--brief-maximal-tension-vs-plyometrics-by-resistance-size`, which now cites it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":573,"cache_read_input_tokens":211468,"output_tokens":1411,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":573},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1411,"cache_read_input_tokens":211468,"cache_creation_input_tokens":573,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":573,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffdNyMc7vLAG4g4XtKNC","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"a1154c4b-7bc9-4c6d-af5b-cb8f584f2dea","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:35:19.892Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
